# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Zola build output
/site/public

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store

# cargo-fuzz
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/corpus
/fuzz/artifacts
/fuzz/Cargo.lock

# Specification downloads (staging area) — ISO 20022 originals, DK/GBIC
# validation subsets and the published example files. They are large and their
# redistribution terms are unclear, so they are never committed. Only the
# individual XSDs the tests need are vendored, into tests/xsd/.
/schemas/*
!/schemas/README.md

# Internal architecture notes (see concepts/README.md).
#
# Anchored to the repository root. These are working documents: they cite the
# rulebooks and the DK subsets by clause, quote the artefacts, and record what
# each design decision cost — none of which is a claim this crate makes to its
# users. `site/` is the public narrative, `CHANGELOG.md` the history and the
# rustdoc the API contract; `concepts/` is none of the three, and nothing in
# the build reads it.
/concepts/
